CORE
main.c
--apply-loop-contracts _ --no-standard-checks
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\[main\.assigns\.\d+\] .*__car_
--
The assigns clause of the second loop is inferred. The may-alias analysis that
the inference uses is computed after the first loop was instrumented, and it
finds that p may alias the __car_lb and __car_ub snapshots of the write set of
the first loop, which point to a as well. Inferred targets that write through
these snapshots, such as *((int *)__car_lb + k), must be removed: they are
spurious, and checking their validity at the head of the second loop failed.
